# Cooldown exemptions for hack/verify-deps.sh.
#
# The cooldown stage refuses any module version whose age is under 14 days:
# most malicious releases are found and pulled within days, so waiting them out
# is a cheap defense. The age is the commit time the module proxy records for
# the version, not when it was first published, so a backdated commit is not
# caught. A version that must be adopted sooner (a security fix, say) is listed
# here after someone has audited it, one per line:
#
#   <module> <version> <reason>
#
# The reason is required. Delete a line once its version is older than the
# cooldown; the script prints a note for every line that no longer matches.
golang.org/x/net v0.60.0 x/net v0.60.0 adopted 2026-10-09 for GO-2026-6611/6612/6617; supply-chain audit 2026-10-11 (two blind auditors + per-module third opinion) found it byte-identical to the upstream tag
